invariant: INV-17
file: src/sha3.c
catches: sha3_equiv_test
reason: shake_absorb never wipes the stack below its body, so the lanes
  and the values of theta that the compiler wrote to stack slots of its
  own stay there after a call that ran the permutation. Under ML-KEM and
  ML-DSA-87 the state comes from a secret seed. Every output is still
  right. bin/sha3_equiv_test, a device object's build, copies the stack
  below each kind of call and finds a lane the call computed from its
  input: under Apple clang on an Apple silicon Mac and under gcc in CI
  (docs/decisions.md 219).

--- old
    absorb(s->lane, s->rate, &s->pos, in, n);
    wipe_below_after(permutes);
--- new
    absorb(s->lane, s->rate, &s->pos, in, n);
    (void)permutes;
